VERSION 1.7.0
------------------------
   o Added use_shared_background mode to Machima2() for explicit
     g_0 (shared bulk background) + delta_c (cell-type deviations)
     decomposition of Hi-C. Addresses bulk-mimicking failure where
     per-cell-type predictions are indistinguishable.
   o Added init_g0, init_delta, lambda_delta, fix_g0 arguments.
   o Added predict_celltype_R() and predict_celltype_delta() in result.
   o Mutually exclusive with lambda_coupling < Inf.

VERSION 1.6.1
------------------------
   o Fixed default initialization of U when lambda_coupling < Inf.
     U_init=0 caused MU dead-zone (U stayed zero throughout training).
     New default: runif(1e-5, 1e-2), small enough to preserve starting
     reconstruction but non-zero for MU to update.

VERSION 1.6.0
------------------------
   o Added lambda_coupling for soft coupling between W_RNA and Hi-C
     basis. When finite, W_E := W_RNA + U is used for Hi-C with
     penalty lambda_coupling * ||U||^2. Default Inf = hard share.
   o Added init_U and fixU arguments.

VERSION 1.5.0
------------------------
   o Added J_hic_only parameter to Machima2() for Hi-C-only basis
     columns (W_hic). Hi-C reconstruction becomes
     G_shared*H_Sym*G_shared^T + W_hic*diag(h_hic)*W_hic^T.
     Default J_hic_only=0 reproduces v1.4.x exactly.
   o Added W_hic_init and fixW_hic arguments.

VERSION 1.4.0
------------------------
   o Added lambda_orthW in [0, 1] to Machima() and Machima2() for
     continuous control of W_RNA column orthogonality (replacing
     binary orthW_RNA toggle). Default 0 = standard NMF.
   o orthW_RNA is now deprecated (still functional, emits warning)

VERSION 1.3.0
------------------------
   o H_Sym_structure="diagonal" now uses proper constrained MU
     (directly on J diagonal entries), replacing ad hoc post-MU
     projection. Yields large fit improvement on Hi-C data.
   o Added lambda_balance to Machima() and Machima2() to control
     relative weight of X_RNA vs X_Epi loss (0=RNA, 0.5=equal, 1=Epi).
     Default 0.5 preserves pre-1.3.0 behaviour.

VERSION 1.2.0
------------------------
   o BREAKING: Machima2() default for fixT changed from FALSE to TRUE.
     Auto-constructs identity T when T=NULL, fixT=TRUE, and l==n.
     Callers relying on learned T must set fixT=FALSE explicitly.
   o Added deprecation warning when fixT=FALSE without T_regularization
   o Added H_Sym_structure = c("symmetric", "diagonal") to Machima2()
     for constraining H_Sym to diagonal core (sym-CP / sym-PARAFAC)

VERSION 1.1.0
------------------------
   o Added T_regularization = "low_rank" (T = U * t(V))
     to structurally bound T capacity and prevent H_Sym collapse
   o Fixed frobenius_unit list-mode crash: use single global RMS
     scalar instead of per-chrom scalars, with eps guard
   o Documented dimnames assignment algorithm in @details
     (background-absorbing "comp_*" components)

VERSION 1.0.0
------------------------
   o Added Machima2() for symmetric epigenomic matrices
     (X_Epi ~ G * H_Sym * t(G), where G = T * W_RNA)
   o Added init_W_RNA/init_H_RNA/init_H_Sym, fixH_Sym to Machima2()
   o Added T_regularization ("frobenius_unit", "l2") to Machima2()
   o Added nmf_init_n_restart/num_iter/algorithm params
   o Exported Mat2List()
   o Fixed NA in dimnames when J > num_celltypes
   o Fixed BetaDivergence formula (operator precedence + X/Y swap)
   o Fixed L1_W_RNA unused in W_RNA updates
   o Fixed horizontal mode RecError mismatch

VERSION 0.99.0
------------------------
   o Package released
